# Recursion Tree / DP Table / Diagram

Not applicable.

This problem uses **prefix preprocessing**, not recursion or dynamic programming.

---

# Why This Works

The preprocessing stores enough prefix information to answer each query without scanning the substring again.

* Prefix sums compute digit sums in O(1).
* Prefix non-zero counts determine the length of the concatenated number.
* Prefix concatenated numbers combined with powers of 10 allow removal of the left prefix in O(1).

Thus every query is answered in constant time after linear preprocessing.

---

# Edge Cases

1. Entire substring is zeros

```text
0000
```

Answer

```text
0
```

---

2. Single digit

```text
7
```

Answer

```text
7×7=49
```

---

3. Single zero

```text
0
```

Answer

```text
0
```

---

4. Query starts at index 0

Need special handling since there is no prefix before index 0.

---

5. Large input

Handled efficiently using prefix arrays.

